{"uid":"modules/loop/decision_log.py","name":"decision_log.py","qualname":"modules/loop/decision_log.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/loop/decision_log.py","line":1,"end_line":270,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Reproducible decision ledger for the autonomous loop.","description":"Every next-action choice the loop makes is recorded here as one bounded\nJSONL row, so an operator can answer \"why did the harness run this?\" and\nre-execute a campaign deterministically. The schema is a decision audit:\ndigests of the decision inputs (the engagement context, the model prompt, the\ndeterministic-relevant config) plus a model-versus-rule fallback flag make each\ndecision auditable without storing raw secrets.\n\nA decision produced by a deterministic selector (:mod:`modules.selection`)\ncarries ``model_fallback=False`` and empty prompt/reply digests; one produced\nby the LLM planner carries ``model_fallback=True`` with both digests set. The\n``filtered`` list names every candidate the harness rejected and the reason,\nso a silently dropped command is never invisible again.\n\nThe ledger is append-only and self-rotating, mirroring\n``modules.lazy_loop.record_worker_traces`` so the two ledgers share one I/O\ndiscipline. Nothing here imports the loop runtime, keeping the module free of\nimport cycles and usable from tests in isolation.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/loop/decision_log.py::DECISIONS_FILE","modules/loop/decision_log.py::digest","modules/loop/decision_log.py::context_digest","modules/loop/decision_log.py::config_digest","modules/loop/decision_log.py::new_run_id","modules/loop/decision_log.py::DecisionRecord","modules/loop/decision_log.py::record","modules/loop/decision_log.py::read_records","modules/loop/decision_log.py::filtered_rows"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
